cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference the AI Usage Scale, please cite it as below."
title: "The AI Usage Scale"
abstract: >-
  An independent, open, six-level vocabulary for declaring how a work was made with generative AI —
  whose substance it carries, and whether a person reviewed it before publication.
  Human-readable and machine-readable, with CC0 definitions and marks.
  Suggested mappings are independent proposals, not institutional endorsements.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Konrad
    family-names: Karauda
  - name: "The AI Usage Scale contributors"
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://usagescale.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/karauda/ai-usage-scale"
keywords:
  - AI disclosure
  - AI transparency
  - generative AI
  - content provenance
  - AI attribution
  - open standard
